.TH BOSWAS-FILES 1 "November 2026" "boswas-apps 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-files \- file manager of Boswas OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-files
.RB [ \-\-new\-window ]
.RB [ \-\-select
.IR path ]...
.RI [ folder ...]
.br
.B boswas-files
.B \-\-version
|
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-files
is Files, the file manager of Boswas OS. A window has tabs, back, forward,
up and refresh buttons, an address bar that shows the path as a breadcrumb
and becomes a text box for typing one, a search box, a command bar, a
navigation pane, the file view, an optional details pane and a status bar.
.PP
The navigation pane lists Home, the user's folders (from
.BR xdg\-user\-dirs (1)),
folders the user pinned, This PC with the volumes of the computer and the
Trash. The file view has a Details layout with sortable, resizable columns
and List, Tiles and four sizes of Icons; image files are shown as
thumbnails in the icon and tile layouts. The layout and the sort order are
the same for every folder and are remembered.
.PP
Copying, moving, deleting, compressing and extracting run in the
background and are shown in a panel with the current file, the items and
bytes done, the speed and a button to cancel. When something with the same
name is in the way, Files asks whether to replace it, skip it or keep both.
What could not be done is listed at the end, item by item. Delete moves to
the Trash; Shift+Delete deletes for good after a confirmation. The last
rename, move, copy, creation and move to the Trash can be undone (Ctrl+Z)
and redone (Ctrl+Y); undoing never overwrites a file and never deletes one
for good.
.PP
A file is opened with the default application of its type, which is found
as the freedesktop.org specifications say (desktop entries and
.IR mimeapps.list ).
A program, a script with the execute permission or a desktop entry is never
started by opening it without a question first.
.PP
Only one instance runs per session. Starting the program again with
folders opens them as tabs of the window that is in front; without
arguments it brings that window forward.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window (with the given folders as its tabs) instead of using
the window that is open.
.TP
.BI \-\-select " path"
Open the folder that holds
.I path
and select
.I path
in it. May be given more than once.
.TP
.I folder
A folder to open: a path, a
.B file:
URL,
.B trash:///
for the Trash or
.B computer:///
for This PC. The path of a file opens its folder with the file selected.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TS
l l.
Ctrl+T, Ctrl+W	New tab, close tab
Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab	Next tab, previous tab
Ctrl+N	New window
Alt+Left, Alt+Right	Back, forward
Alt+Up, Backspace	Up one folder
F5, Ctrl+R	Refresh
Ctrl+L, Alt+D	Type a path in the address bar
Ctrl+F, Ctrl+E, F3	Search the folder and its subfolders
Enter	Open
Alt+Enter	Properties
F2	Rename
Delete, Shift+Delete	Move to the Trash, delete for good
Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V	Cut, copy, paste
Ctrl+Shift+C	Copy as path
Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y	Undo, redo
Ctrl+A	Select all
Ctrl+Shift+N	New folder
Ctrl+H	Show or hide hidden files
Ctrl+Shift+1 ... 7	Extra large, large, medium, small icons, List, Details, Tiles
Alt+Shift+P	Details pane
Ctrl+,	Settings
F11	Full screen
.TE
.PP
While dragging files, dropping on the same volume moves and dropping on
another volume copies; Ctrl makes it a copy and Shift a move.
.SH D-BUS
While it runs,
.B boswas-files
owns the name
.B org.freedesktop.FileManager1
on the session bus and implements
.BR ShowFolders ,
.B ShowItems
and
.BR ShowItemProperties ,
which other applications call for "Show in folder". The name is not taken
from another file manager that owns it.
.PP
Volumes are mounted, unmounted, ejected and unlocked through
.BR udisksd (8)
(UDisks2) on the system bus, which asks for authorisation itself when it
is needed. Without UDisks2 the mounted volumes are listed and cannot be
changed from Files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.Files/settings.json
The settings: hidden files, extensions, single or double click, the view,
the sort order, the start folder, the pinned folders, pane and column
widths.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.Files/window.ini
The size of the window.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mimeapps.list
Written when an application is chosen with "Always use this app".
.TP
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash ", " $topdir/.Trash/$uid ", " $topdir/.Trash\-$uid
The Trash, as the freedesktop.org Trash specification 1.0 lays it out. The
optional
.I directorysizes
cache is not written.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails
Thumbnails, shared with other programs as the freedesktop.org thumbnail
specification says (sizes
.I normal
and
.IR large ;
failures in
.IR fail/boswas\-files ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/user\-dirs.dirs
Read for the user's folders in the navigation pane.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, also when the request was handed to the running instance; 2
for wrong options; 4 when started as root, which Files refuses.
.SH NOTES
Archives: "Compress to ZIP" writes ZIP files; "Extract all" reads ZIP and
tar archives (plain, gzip, bzip2, xz) into a new folder and refuses members
that would be written outside it. Password-protected ZIP files are not
supported. Hard links and sparse files are copied as ordinary files;
ownership is not copied.
.PP
Terminal: "Open in Terminal" starts
.B boswas\-terminal \-\-working\-directory
.IR dir ,
or
.B konsole \-\-workdir
.I dir
when that is not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-user\-dirs (1),
.BR udisksctl (1),
.BR boswas\-terminal (1)
